course: dictionary
lesson: 952
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Bloom» can name a flower, or it can be a verb meaning to open into flowers. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «Once they bloom most stop and face east, where the morning sun warms them.» The sentence is about plants turning towards the sun, so bloom means open into flowers. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Bloom can also mean to grow healthy, happy or confident. A shy character can bloom into a confident one. In science, an algal bloom is a sudden big growth of algae in water. Each meaning fits a different kind of text.
fact: Bloom can be a noun (a bloom, a flower) or a verb (to bloom, to open into flowers or grow healthy and confident).
fact: «Lime trees, lypa, bloom in early summer» means the lime trees open their flowers in early summer.
fact: An algal bloom is a sudden big growth of algae in water, and it can be harmful. It can make lakes unsafe for swimming.
fact: In full bloom means completely open with flowers. A late bloomer is someone who develops later than most others.
fact: «Blooming» is an old-fashioned, informal word used in the UK to mean very or annoying, as in «blooming cheek!»
exercise: «Longer, unmown grass lets clover, daisies and other flowers bloom and feed bees.» What does bloom mean here? | To cut down | To shout loudly | To fall over | *To open into flowers
exercise: Ella was shy at first, but over the year she bloomed into a confident speaker. What does bloomed mean here? | Fell asleep | Turned bright red | Ran away from school | *Grew confident and happy
exercise: Scientists warned that the lake had an algal bloom, so swimming was not safe. What is an algal bloom? | A bunch of flowers in a vase | A large group of birds | *A sudden big growth of algae in water | A type of fish
test: Dad says, «What a blooming nuisance!» What does blooming mean here? | *Very annoying | Very hungry | Very beautiful | Very quiet
test: Which phrase means completely open with flowers? | *In full bloom | Algal bloom | A blooming nuisance | A late bloomer
exam: Pick the best meaning of bloom in: «Lime trees bloom in early summer, and bees make honey from them.» | To be painted | To fall to the ground | To grow taller than the bees | *To open into flowers
